  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through Wednesday)\nIssued at 1207 AM CDT Thu Jun 25 2026\n\nThe forecast remains benign through at least the middle of next\nweek. An upper level ridge will remain the primary influence over\nour day to day weather through the next 7 days. By early next week\nthe center of the ridge axis shifts to the east of our area in\nresponse to a deepening upper level trough over the western U.S.\nNevertheless, we will maintain a generally hot and dry forecast.\nWe may be close to heat advisory criteria on Friday and into the\nweekend across portions of the Big Country where temperatures may\nreach 104-106 degrees. For the rest of west central Texas highs\nwill climb into the upper 90s to near 103 degrees Friday though\nSunday. The status quo will continue into the beginning of next\nweek, with highs on Monday and Tuesday in the triple digits.",
